## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Thứ Năm: 3 câu hỏi phỏng vấn

**Q1. "Walk me through your password reset flow."**
> *"Request comes in with an email. If the account exists I generate 32 random bytes with a cryptographic RNG, store the hash of it with a fifteen minute expiry, and email the raw value. Either way — account or no account — I return the same message and the same status code.*
> *The token is single use. When it's redeemed I update the password, mark the token used, and revoke every session for that user, all in one transaction. That last part matters: if the reset was triggered because someone else got into the account, changing the password has to kick them out."*

**Q2. "How do you prevent user enumeration?"**
> *"There are six paths and I went through all of them. Same message on registration, same message on login, same message on reset. Same status code everywhere. And two timing paths — I always run the password hash even when there's no user, and I send the reset email asynchronously so the response time doesn't depend on whether an email went out. I measured both and they're within a few milliseconds."*

**Q3. "Why write auth yourself?"**
> *[Nói bản đã tập ở trên. Đây là câu quan trọng nhất trong ba câu.]*

**5 từ mới:**

| Từ / cụm | Nghĩa | Câu mẫu |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `redeem` (v) | dùng, đổi lấy | *When the token is redeemed.* |
| `single use` | dùng một lần | *The token is single use.* |
| `trigger` (v) | kích hoạt, gây ra | *If the reset was triggered by someone else.* |
| `timing path` | đường có khác biệt thời gian | *There are two timing paths.* |
| `within a few milliseconds` | chênh nhau vài mili giây | *They're within a few milliseconds.* |

